---
config:
  theme: base
  fontFamily: "Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 24
    width: 130
    diagramMarginX: 10
    boxMargin: 12
    boxTextMargin: 8
    messageMargin: 40
    noteMargin: 22
    labelBoxWidth: 56
    labelBoxHeight: 28
    messageFontSize: 16
    actorFontSize: 16
    noteFontSize: 15
    wrap: false
  themeVariables:
    textColor: "#8b5cf6"
    actorBkg: "#ede9fe"
    actorBorder: "#7c3aed"
    actorTextColor: "#4c1d95"
    actorLineColor: "#a78bfa"
    signalColor: "#8b949e"
    signalTextColor: "#6e7781"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#ccfbf1"
    labelBoxBorderColor: "#0d9488"
    labelTextColor: "#134e4a"
    loopTextColor: "#0d9488"
    noteBkgColor: "#fef3c7"
    noteBorderColor: "#d97706"
    noteTextColor: "#78350f"
    activationBkgColor: "#c4b5fd"
    activationBorderColor: "#7c3aed"
    mainBkg: "#ede9fe"
    nodeBorder: "#7c3aed"
    secondaryColor: "#ede9fe"
    secondaryBorderColor: "#7c3aed"
    secondaryTextColor: "#4c1d95"
    tertiaryColor: "#ede9fe"
    tertiaryBorderColor: "#7c3aed"
    tertiaryTextColor: "#4c1d95"
  themeCSS: >
    svg, .label, .nodeLabel, .edgeLabel, foreignObject div { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; }
    .actor { filter: drop-shadow(0 3px 6px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.18)); }
    rect.actor { rx: 12px; ry: 12px; }
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant JTC as Trajectory<br/>controller
    participant HW as StepitHardware
    participant Drv as DefaultDriver
    participant MCU as Teensy firmware
    loop every cycle, 30 Hz
        HW->>Drv: read(): get_status()
        Drv->>MCU: Status 0x75
        MCU-->>Drv: 0x11, 5 x id, position,<br/>velocity, distance
        Drv-->>HW: motor states
        Note over HW: copy each state to<br/>the joint of its id
        HW-->>JTC: state interfaces
        JTC->>HW: command.position<br/>of each joint
        HW->>Drv: write(): set_position()
        Drv->>MCU: Move 0x71, id and<br/>position per joint
        Note over MCU: set the goals under<br/>writingMotorGoals
        MCU-->>Drv: 0x11
    end
    Note over MCU: the interrupt steps each motor<br/>to its goal at its acceleration
